From: handheld-extra
Subject: [PATCH] reshade: give an effect without uniforms a uniform buffer

ReshadeEffectPipeline::init() sizes the uniform buffer by the effect's
uniforms. An effect that declares none (every value a #define) asks for a
zero-size VkBuffer, which is invalid, and Turnip then segfaults in
vkBindBufferMemory, taking the whole session down. Selecting such an effect
through GAMESCOPE_RESHADE_EFFECT restarted Game Mode on the AYN Odin 3
(Adreno 830, Mesa 26.2.5) every time, 2026-10-24; effects with uniforms
were unaffected.

Give the buffer a 16-byte floor. Nothing reads past total_uniform_size, so
the extra bytes go unused.

Present in ValveSoftware and OpenGamingCollective gamescope as of 2026-10-24.

---
--- a/src/reshade_effect_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/reshade_effect_manager.cpp
@@ -1020,7 +1020,9 @@
         VkBufferCreateInfo bufferCreateInfo =
         {
             .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_BUFFER_CREATE_INFO,
-            .size  = m_module->total_uniform_size,
+            // An effect without uniforms has none to size it by, and a zero-size
+            // buffer is invalid: Turnip segfaults binding its memory.
+            .size  = std::max<VkDeviceSize>(m_module->total_uniform_size, 16),
             .usage = VK_BUFFER_USAGE_UNIFORM_BUFFER_BIT,
         };
 
